(1295, 'Test', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'scientific', 'official edition', 'biography', '', '', '', ''),
(1296, 'Kumanan', 'Antony', '', 'Jesus my true friend', 'Bangalore', '', '', '2006', '5', '', '', '', '', 'engl', 'scientific', 'digital', 'Schoenstatt', 'Jesus a true friend, forgiver, trustworthy, Kentenich, love', 'Being a shepherd, Jesus expressed his parental love. We are called to share this parental love and to distribute it to the people of God. We are called to be a powerful defense (Sir 6:14) that protects people from the cultures of evil and from psychological disorders. We are called to be instruments to impart his parental love. Filial love: With childlike spirit we completely surrender to God to show that we completely depend on God’s friendship and love. Sacrificial love: Jesus’ sacrifice on the cross would be the highest of all the sacrifices. That is what we remember in our everyday Eucharist celebr¬ation and “He is silently close to us in every situation.” It is extremely difficult to die for a friend. But that is exactly what Jesus did. Jesus did not talk about his love but proved it. What is our sacrificial love to him? That is nothing but blank-cheque surrender by which we entirely offer ourselves to God to be used as instruments to build a new world. Friendship love: Emerson tells us, that “the only way to have a friend is to be one.” To be one means that they share freely mutual love, are open-minded, correct the drawbacks of each other and consider each other equal. It is more easy to share all our difficulties to Jesus as our friend than to Jesus as an almighty powerful God. Through this personal relationship we become one with Him. \r\n	As a whole my idea is that friendship love should also include parental love, filial love, and sacrificial love. Then only friendship receives its fullness, as a quote from B. Franklin states, “A brother may not be a friend but a friend will always be a brother.”\r\n', '', 'Author'),
(1297, 'test', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'scientific', 'official edition', 'biography', '', 'test', '', ''),
(1298, 'test', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'scientific', 'official edition', 'biography', '', 'Being a shepherd, Jesus expressed his parental love. We are called to share this parental love and to distribute it to the people of God. We are called to be a powerful defense (Sir 6:14) that protects people from the cultures of evil and from psychological disorders. We are called to be instruments to impart his parental love. Filial love: With childlike spirit we completely surrender to God to show that we completely depend on God’s friendship and love. Sacrificial love: Jesus’ sacrifice on the cross would be the highest of all the sacrifices. That is what we remember in our everyday Eucharist celebr¬ation and “He is silently close to us in every situation.” It is extremely difficult to die for a friend. But that is exactly what Jesus did. Jesus did not talk about his love but proved it. What is our sacrificial love to him? That is nothing but blank-cheque surrender by which we entirely offer ourselves to God to be used as instruments to build a new world. Friendship love: Emerson tells us, that “the only way to have a friend is to be one.” To be one means that they share freely mutual love, are open-minded, correct the drawbacks of each other and consider each other equal. It is more easy to share all our difficulties to Jesus as our friend than to Jesus as an almighty powerful God. Through this personal relationship we become one with Him. \r\n	As a whole my idea is that friendship love should also include parental love, filial love, and sacrificial love. Then only friendship receives its fullness, as a quote from B. Franklin states, “A brother may not be a friend but a friend will always be a brother.”\r\n', '', ''),
(1299, 'Brügger', 'Franz Johannes', '', 'Die apostolische Familienbewegung von Schönstatt   Zum Selbstverständnis der Familienliga  Die Mitglieder', 'Vallendar-Schönstatt', 'Herausgegeben vom Sekretariat der Schönstatt-Familienliga', 'erste', '2003', '16 Seiten', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'non scientific', 'self edition', 'family', '', 'Es geht um eine gemeinsame Orientierung sowohl der Mitarbdeiter an der Zentrale als auch der Verantwortlichen der Familienliga in den Diözesen an den Hörder Satzungen im Blick auf die MITGLIEDERWEIHE in der Familienliga. Die vier Kapitel bieten jeweils eine knappe thematische Abhandlung zu einem Aspekt der Mitgliederweihe,einen entsprechenden Text aus dem Neuen Testament und dessen Auslegung im Blick auf den Aspekt der in dem Kapitel behandelten Thematik. Die Kapitelüberschriften nach einem Vorwort sind: Apostolat - Liebesbündnis - Weg - Anregungen.Den Abschluss bilden die Hörder Satzungen in der Fassung letzten von P. Josef Kentenich aus dem Jahr 1935. Die Schrift kann über das Sekretariat der Schönstatt-Familienliga, Höhrer Str., Haus der Familie, \r\n56179 Vallendar-Schönstatt bezogen werden. Eine englische Übersetzung ist in Vorbereitung.', '', ''),
(1300, 'Brügger', 'Franz Johannes', '', 'Familienpastoral      Reflektierte Erfahrung aus der Schönstatt-Bewegung', 'Vallendar-Schönstatt', 'Patris Verlag', 'Erste', '2004', '340 Seiten', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'scientific', 'official edition', 'family', '', 'In diesem Buch reflektiert der Autor die Pastoralerfahrung der Schönstatt-Bewegung. Damit wird ein detaillierter Einblick in eine geistliche Bewegung möglich, aber auch das Gespräch angeregt über Grundsätze und Prinzipien einer Ehe- und Familienpastorl, die durch Spiritualität und Pädagogik Schönstatts ihr Profil hat.\r\nDas Buch richtet sich an Priester und Laien im pastoralen Dienst, an Mitglieder anderer Geistlicher Bewegungen, sowie an alle, die an Information über die Schönstatt-Bewegung interessiert sind. Das Vorwort schrieb Manfred Entrich OP, Leiter des Bereichs Pastoral der deutschen Bischofskonferenz.', '', ''),
(1301, 'Schönstatt-Familienbewegung, Herausgeber', '', 'Sr. Annetraud Bolkart, P. Franz Joh. Brügger', 'Familienliederbuch, Miteinander wachsen  -  dem Himmel entgegen', 'Vallendar-Schönstatt', 'WEGA Verlag GmbH, Mainz', '3000', '2004', '295 Lieder', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'non scientific', 'official edition', 'family', '', '', '', ''),
(1303, 'Schönstatt-Studentenbewegung, Herausgeber', '', 'Autorenteam unter Leitung von P. Franz Joh. Brügger, Vallendar und Konstantin Blumers, Mainz', 'Ich will Wahrheit  Ich will Freiheit  Ich will Verantwortung  Ein Studienbegleiter', 'Freiburg Basel Wien', 'Herder', '13 000', '1981', '48 Seiten', '', '', '', '', 'deu', 'non scientific', 'official edition', 'youth', 'Antwort auf den marxistischen \\"Studienführer\\" Ende der 70er Jahre', '', '', ''),
