(4571, 2643, 'en_US', 'This field can be used for determining personal precedence as mentioned in Constitutions no. 156 (text below). “Personal precedence is determined first of all by date of first incorporation into the community, then by date of ordination to the priesthood, then by date of birth. Founding members dispensed of the novitiate in the first years after our founding hold the personal precedence determined for them by the first General Chapter.” (cf. GK 1974, p. 142).', '5', '2016-10-06 12:47:15'),
(4572, 2644, 'en_US', 'Pre-community membership date', '11', '2016-10-06 08:06:49'),
(4573, 2643, 'es_ES', 'Este campo puede ser utilizado para determinar la precedencia personal como mencionado en Constituciones #156 (texto abajo). "La precedencia personal está determinada en primer lugar por los anos de pertenencia a la Comunidad, a continuación por los anos de sacerdocio, después por los anos de vida. Para los miembros fundadores que en los primeros anos después de la fundación del Instituto fueron dispensados del noviciado, vale la precedencia personal que fue determinada por el primer Capítulo de nuestra Familia." (CG 74, pág. 142)', '5', '2016-10-06 12:47:15'),
(4574, 2643, 'de_DE', 'This field can be used for determining personal precedence as mentioned in Constitutions no. 156 (text below). “Personal precedence is determined first of all by date of first incorporation into the community, then by date of ordination to the priesthood, then by date of birth. Founding members dispensed of the novitiate in the first years after our founding hold the personal precedence determined for them by the first General Chapter.” (cf. GK 1974, p. 142).', '5', '2016-10-06 12:47:15'),
(4575, 2643, 'pt_BR', 'This field can be used for determining personal precedence as mentioned in Constitutions no. 156 (text below). “Personal precedence is determined first of all by date of first incorporation into the community, then by date of ordination to the priesthood, then by date of birth. Founding members dispensed of the novitiate in the first years after our founding hold the personal precedence determined for them by the first General Chapter.” (cf. GK 1974, p. 142).', '5', '2016-10-06 12:47:15'),
